WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.537
Each Microsoft 365 cloud
has its own Graph host.

2
00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:08.850
GCC keeps the worldwide endpoint,
graph dot microsoft dot com,

3
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.725
and signs in with the Global environment.

4
00:00:11.725 --> 00:00:13.575
That's the workbook's baseline.

5
00:00:13.575 --> 00:00:18.884
As a side note, GCC High uses graph
dot microsoft dot U S, and DoD uses

6
00:00:18.884 --> 00:00:24.587
dod dash graph dot microsoft dot U S,
each with its own environment name.

7
00:00:24.587 --> 00:00:27.833
The A P I is available
on the national clouds,

8
00:00:27.833 --> 00:00:32.612
and each list method's table shows
U S Government L four and L five.

9
00:00:32.612 --> 00:00:34.187
The kit has two guards.

10
00:00:34.187 --> 00:00:37.303
Before the first call, it
compares the Graph session's

11
00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:41.126
environment and tenant with the
settings, and refuses a mismatch.

12
00:00:41.126 --> 00:00:43.854
And a next link is a U
R L the response chose,

13
00:00:43.854 --> 00:00:47.787
so the kit follows it only if it's
on the cloud's own Graph host.

14
00:00:47.787 --> 00:00:49.439
Anything else is refused,

15
00:00:49.439 --> 00:00:53.280
so the token never goes somewhere
the agency didn't choose.
